WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.900
A man at a desk, far
from New York, writing.

2
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:09.810
Behind him, faint across dark water,
a lit mansion and a small green light.

3
00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.260
The pages slide into a stack.

4
00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:15.590
He's writing it all down
two years after it happened.

5
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.250
And he hands us his credentials: "I am
one of the few honest people that I have

6
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.470
ever known."

7
00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.350
He's the one holding the pen.

8
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.410
So should you trust him?

9
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:29.710
In this mission, you'll work out where
Nick stands in the story he tells, looking

10
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:30.610
back.

11
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.640
You'll test his opening promise
to "reserve all judgements".

12
00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:38.540
And you'll watch him choose when
we find things out about Gatsby.

13
00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:41.720
Your mission: decide whether
you should trust Nick.
